The reconstructed positive claim closed with exit 0 and `#Top`. Static review confirms that it runs the structurally identical submitted MPY term at each integer 1–1000 and blocks unless the returned tuple equals independently computed palindrome counts. I also found one non-fatal semantics limitation: its unguarded `//` and `%` equations disagree with Python for negative operands, but no negative operand or divisor is reachable for any valid input; I’m treating this as an over-broad language-model concern, not a false proof witness on the theorem’s domain.
